{"name":"Sports Fan","hex":"#e08119","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sports fan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A familiar form of address, a jocular term of endearment.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see sports,‎ fan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sports_fan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sports fandom","blocks":[{"text":"Sports fandom is the community of fans sharing interests in sports, particularly spectator sports."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Mora_IK_vs_Leksand_in_Stockholm_2013-01-05_14.jpg/330px-Mora_IK_vs_Leksand_in_Stockholm_2013-01-05_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sports_fandom"},{"title":"Fan (person)","blocks":[{"text":"A fan or fanatic, sometimes also termed an aficionado or enthusiast, is a person who exhibits strong interest or admiration for something or somebody, such as a celebrity, a sport, a sports team, a genre, a politician, a book, a television show, a movie, a video game or an entertainer. Collectively, the fans of a particular object or person constitute its fanbase or fandom. They may show their enthusiasm in a variety of ways, such as by promoting the object of their interest, being members of a related fan club, holding or participating in fan conventions or writing fan mail. They may also engage in creative activities such as creating fanzines, writing fan fiction, making memes, drawing fan art, or developing fan games. Some excessively avid fans are called \"stans\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Rock_en_Parque_Roca_%286796076495%29.jpg/330px-Rock_en_Parque_Roca_%286796076495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fan_(person)"},{"title":"Sport","blocks":[{"text":"A sport is a physical activity or game, often competitive and organised, that maintains or improves physical ability and skills. Sport may provide enjoyment to participants and entertainment to spectators. The number of participants in a particular sport can vary from hundreds of people to a single individual."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Youth-soccer-indiana.jpg/330px-Youth-soccer-indiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sport"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Berkan_Karabulut_-_Yellow_Fenerbah%C3%A7e_20250131.jpg/500px-Berkan_Karabulut_-_Yellow_Fenerbah%C3%A7e_20250131.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Berkan_Karabulut_-_Yellow_Fenerbah%C3%A7e_20250131.jpg/1280px-Berkan_Karabulut_-_Yellow_Fenerbah%C3%A7e_20250131.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Berkan_Karabulut_-_Yellow_Fenerbah%C3%A7e_20250131.jpg/500px-Berkan_Karabulut_-_Yellow_Fenerbah%C3%A7e_20250131.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The mascot of Fenerbahçe Basketball, Yellow, with Fenerbahçe S.K. supporters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABerkan_Karabulut_-_Yellow_Fenerbah%C3%A7e_20250131.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/200001-235-XL_%286168040935%29.jpg/500px-200001-235-XL_%286168040935%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/200001-235-XL_%286168040935%29.jpg/500px-200001-235-XL_%286168040935%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American college football supporters of the Connecticut Huskies in a 2011 game against the Iowa State Cyclones.","link":"https://